# Repo-root .env — read by `docker compose` for variable interpolation ONLY.
# Copy to `.env` if you need any of the values below. The application's own
# configuration lives in backend/.env (generated by `make setup`), NOT here.
#
# Nothing in this file is required for a normal `docker compose up -d --build`.

# ── ngrok tunnel (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed for `make tunnel`, which exposes the local backend on a public
# HTTPS URL for TradingView webhook testing. Get a token at https://ngrok.com.
NGROK_AUTHTOKEN=

# ── IB Gateway sidecar (PARKED — Alpaca pivot, ADR-041) ──────────────────────
# The parked IBKR sidecar is opt-in only (`docker compose --profile ibkr up
# ib-gateway`). Its interpolation variables are documented in docker-compose.yml
# under the `ib-gateway` service; set them there if you revive that path. They
# are deliberately omitted here so this file stays free of broker credentials.
